Quantum systems, here the conduction electron gas, are made up of entities that occupy discrete states. These discrete levels are modified in an excited state such as a plasmon. As extreme plasmons are sustained by strong excitation of quantum electron gas, the statistical distribution of electron states significantly diverges from the initial Fermi-Dirac statistics, making linear theory inapplicable. A quantum kinetic framework is, thus, put forth here to account for this. 

